     "annotations": [],
     "text": "Several Munich bakeries sell sourdough bread (*Sauerteigbrot*), including:\n\n- **Hofpfisterei** — A Munich institution specializing in organic sourdough breads made with a traditional three-stage sourdough process. Multiple locations across the city.\n- **Julius Brantner Brothandwerk** — Artisan bakery with locations in Schwabing, Altstadt, and Haidhausen; known for its signature **Brothandwerk 25** sourdough.\n- **Bageri** — Scandinavian-inspired bakery at **Tumblingerstraße 45, 80337 München**, offering wheat- and rye-sourdough breads.\n- **Suuapinga Bakery** — Bakery in Glockenbach making sourdough loaves, rolls, and pastries.\n- **Rischart** — Large Munich bakery chain with numerous branches; sells naturally leavened sourdough bread.\n- **Familienbäckerei Kistenpfennig** — Several Munich locations; tested products include sourdough bread and rye-crust loaves.\n- **Bäckerei REIS** — Organic bakery in southern Munich, including Solln and Forstenried, offering fresh sourdough breads.\n- **Brotatelier, Brotraum, Zeit für Brot, Neulinger, and Cumpanum** — Also frequently recommended locally for sourdough, though availability can vary by day.\n\nFor the most specialist sourdough selection, start with **Julius Brantner, Bageri, Suuapinga, or Hofpfisterei**. Bread availability and opening hours can change, so it’s worth checking the bakery’s website or social media before visiting.",
